e but to fully complete his  arc he must pick himself up and start  again now armed with the knowledge of  his past flaws it takes his friends to  motivate him to run but there's one  problem how the hell is he supposed to  take on a seasoned incumbent like Dede  Standish q Astrid she's moved to New  York after sending her father to jail  while on a catering gig she noticed  senator Standish and her love affair  with two men she's in a throuple armed  with this knowledge and mcafee belief  that if Payton focuses on a single  relatable issue he might just stand a  chance at taking down the senator but  what really makes Payton all-in is his  final talk with the ghosts of River  River provided the ultimate foil for  Payton whereas Payton was calculated  mechanical River was authentic from the  heart and grounded throughout the season  Payton is visited by rivers ghosts as a  means to have his character grow and  learn river kept him in check  after visiting Payton in the bar he  tells them that there's more honor in  defeat than an unused potential leading  Payton to agree to run against senator  Standish Alice upon hearing that Payton  is taking the plunge leaves her own  wedding in order to be by his side her  love for Payton is so strong she faked a  cheating scandal in order to boost  Payton's poll numbers for the high  school election it will be interesting  to see what lengths she's willing to go  for pain and the campaign next season  campaigns also happen to cost a lot of  money luckily there are a lot of places  Payton could look to bankroll his  campaign  Astra's family Alice's an arrangement  with his own father or even the Chinese  but what the show doesn't really delve  into that deeply is why Payton wants to  be President so deeply why has he spent  every waking moment to this one pursuit  the answer lies in his upbringing Payton  was adopted and never knew why his  biological parents abandoned him  what better way to gain a feeling of  acceptance than by winning an election a  way to prove that you are wanted I  wouldn't be surprised if Payton's true  birth parents came into the picture in  future episodes as well and here's a  crazy tinfoil hat conspiracy what if  Dede Standish is Payton's biological  mother that could be absolutely crazy  speaking of family will gwyneth paltrow  reprise her role as Payton's mother  she's off in Boonton which just so  happens to border Chinese controlled  Tibet yet another way the writers could  link China to Payton's campaign but what  I'm more curious about is how Payton's  campaign will differ from his high  school one will the team continue and  anything it takes approach to winning or  will it be more reserved seeing as how  this season had many over-the-top  elements my guess is that we'll be in  for more of the same this time with even  more at stake in what will happen to  Jessica Lange and will we see her return  as dusty Jackson when asked by  Entertainment Weekly if we'll see dusty  again she replied quote I don't think so  I mean Dusty's not one of those that has  a second act end quote  so it looks like this might be the last  we see of her finally I want to talk  about one of  more interesting episodes number 5 the  voter which almost exclusively follows  one character as they go through  Election Day it's this episode that  shines a light on voter apathy and the  feeling that our votes don't make a  difference affect us or that those who  are in charge simply don't have our  well-being at heart we follow Elliott  Beach Minh and apathetic undecided voter  who asked heard and Peyton tried to get  to vote for them they don't actually  care about him as a person they just  want his vote which speaks to what many  Americans believe in the 2016 election  almost half of eligible voters didn't  even vote when asked if he voted Elliott  says that his vote doesn't even matter  this is especially interesting because  we find out later from the principal  that Payton lost by two votes one that  could have been Elliott's and this girl  whose vote was suppressed because she  didn't have her student ID but at the  core of what the writers are trying to  say here is not that people are dumb for  not voting it's that the politicians in  charge treat them as votes and not as  people that no matter who they vote for  things won't change if we can instill in  them a reason to vote to get behind a  candidate maybe some real change can  happen the politician season two is  shaping up to be even bigger than season  one with a huge shift from high school  campaign to the US Senate with such a  huge shift it'll be interesting to see  where the new season goes and what this  could mean for our characters I hope you  enjoyed this video be sure to LIKE and  subscribe with the Belon as I have more  videos coming away you can also follow  me on Twitter at big story whitey  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much

